README for Windows (32- and 64-bit) platforms
---------------------------------------------

**Compilers**
BZFlag uses Microsoft Visual C++ 2017 for its prebuilt binary releases, and
project files are provided for it. The solution files are located inside of
the MSVC directory. You can download Visual Studio Community 2017 for free:
  https://aka.ms/vs/15/release/vs_community.exe

**Targets**
There are a total of 4 build targets in the VC projects. There are targets
for Release and Debug, and each has a 32-bit (Win32) and 64-bit (x64) version.
Only Win32 is actively supported as x64 compilation was only recently made
possible. The x64 compilation does emit some warnings, so it will fail to
compile in Debug mode until those are resolved.

**Required Dependencies**
Several third-party dependencies are required to compile BZFlag. We have a
CMake build process located in the dependencies directory to download and
compile all of these. You will need to install CMake from:
  https://cmake.org/download/

After CMake is installed, run buildVC2017.bat in the dependencies directory.

**Running and Debugging**
By default the compiler will copy the compiled executables to the root level
of the source drive (the same place that the data dir is at). From there
you can simply double click the application to run it. If you wish to debug
the program, you must set the debug executable path and working directory
inside VC to use this executable and path.

**Installer**
If you wish to build the full release package using the fullbuild solution,
you will need to have NSIS installed. The built installer will be placed in
the bin_Release folder for the target in the root of the source tree. Install
NSIS from:
  http://nsis.sourceforge.net/
